# Astro Style Conventions

This rule applies to all `.astro` files in the project.

## SCSS Usage and Variables

- **Always use SCSS** for styling in `<style>` blocks within Astro components
- **Reference CSS custom properties from [global.scss](mdc:src/styles/global.scss)** for consistent theming:
  - Use `var(--main-width)` for max-width constraints
  - Use spacing variables: `var(--spacing-xxlg)`, `var(--spacing-xlg)`, `var(--spacing-lg)`, `var(--spacing-md)`, `var(--spacing-sm)`
  - Use color variables: `var(--bg-color)`, `var(--text-color)`, `var(--secondary-text-color)`, `var(--blue-color)`, `var(--gray-color)`, etc.
  - Use font variables: `var(--roboto)`, `var(--roboto-condensed)`, `var(--roboto-mono)`
  - Use `var(--font-size-md)` for consistent text sizing
  - Use `var(--border-radius-xsm)` for consistent border radius

## Class Naming Conventions

- **Do NOT use BEM methodology** (no double underscores `__` or double hyphens `--`)
- **Use short, descriptive class names** that clearly indicate the component or element purpose
- Examples from existing code:
  - `.header`, `.title`, `.hero`, `.main-content`
  - `.blog-post-card`, `.blog-post-card-title`, `.blog-post-card-image`
  - `.polaroid`, `.polaroid-img`, `.polaroid-shine`

## SCSS Structure and Patterns

- **Use nested selectors** to keep styles organized and scoped to the component
- **Group related styles** together within the parent selector
- **Use media queries inside selectors** for responsive design
- **Leverage CSS custom properties** for dynamic theming (light/dark mode support)

## Example Structure

```scss
<style>
  .component-name {
    // Base styles using CSS custom properties
    max-width: var(--main-width);
    padding: var(--spacing-md);
    color: var(--text-color);
    
    .child-element {
      font-family: var(--roboto-condensed);
      font-size: var(--font-size-md);
    }
    
    // Responsive styles
    @media (min-width: 480px) {
      .child-element {
        font-size: 24px;
      }
    }
  }
</style>
```
